      ":question/id": "70f6a99d-5537-535c-b755-8b23026e0cd9",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned} & x + 2 y - z=4 \\\\ & - 2 x - 3 y + 2 z=-3 \\\\ & 2 x + 3 y - z=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 & -11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
