      ":question/id": "560bec7c-68cb-5811-afb6-5876b212b3e1",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned} & x - y + 2 z=-41 \\\\ & 3 x - 2 y + 6 z=-113 \\\\ & - 2 x + 2 y - z=52\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -41 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -113 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 52\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -41 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -113 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 52\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -41 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 & 52\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -41 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -30\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 & -41 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & -21 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -11 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
